title: Bioinformatic workflow for conotoxin discovery and annotation
message: >-
  If you use this workflow, please cite it using the metadata below, and also
  cite the individual tools it orchestrates (see the Citing section of the
  README).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ricardo
    family-names: Gómez-Reyes
    email: rgomez41@uabc.edu.mx
    affiliation: Universidad Autónoma de Baja California (UABC)
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'   # add yours
repository-code: 'https://github.com/rjegr/conotoxin-discovery-workflow'
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, portable Snakemake workflow that discovers and annotates
  conotoxin precursors from single- or paired-end venom-duct RNA-seq. It
  performs read quality control with fastp, replicate-aware de novo assembly
  with Trinity, rnaSPAdes and RNA-Bloom, reference-free contig filtering with
  TransRate, ORF prediction with TransDecoder, cross-assembler dereplication
  with MMseqs2, conotoxin precursor recognition with ConoSorter, secretion
  signal screening with SignalP 6, and homology annotation against the
  ConoServer, NCBI and UniProt Conidae protein databases. Candidates are
  assigned to four confidence tiers based on the level of agreement among four
  independent evidence sources. The workflow runs unchanged on macOS with
  Docker and on Linux HPC under SLURM with Apptainer.
keywords:
  - conotoxin
  - conopeptide
  - Conus
  - venom
  - transcriptomics
  - RNA-seq
  - de novo assembly
  - functional annotation
  - Snakemake
  - reproducible research
  - FAIR
